## 3. Third-Party Services and Advertising

We partner with third-party service providers who may collect information used to identify your device:

### Google AdMob (Google LLC)
The App displays advertisements provided by Google AdMob. Google AdMob may automatically collect and process certain data, including:
- **Device and Advertising Identifiers:** Google Advertising ID (GAID / AAID), IP address, and unique device identifiers.
- **Device Information:** Device model, operating system version, carrier, and network connection type.
- **Ad Interaction Data:** Views, clicks, impressions, and diagnostic/performance data.

AdMob uses this data to serve relevant ads, measure ad performance, prevent fraud, and adhere to user consent standards (e.g., GDPR in the EEA and UK, and CPRA/CCPA in the US). Users can manage ad personalization through their Android device settings under **Settings > Google > Ads**.

For more details on how Google handles data, please review:
- [Google Privacy & Terms](https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads)
- [How Google uses information from sites or apps that use our services](https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites)

### Google Play In-App Billing
If you purchase premium features or an ad-free upgrade:
- All transactions are processed directly by **Google Play** through the Google Play Billing API.
- We receive only confirmation tokens and purchase status from Google to unlock your features.
- We do not have access to your credit card number, bank details, or billing address.
- Please refer to [Google Play’s Privacy Policy](https://policies.google.com/privacy) for details on transaction data handling.

